            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0172" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5638</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-30T13:00:00+02:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 30, 1917, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 2, 12.45 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1453. British Ambassador writes calling conference of Allied representatives on
                    July 4, 5 p.m., on request of Henderson to consider <pb facs="0173" n="99"
                        xml:id="pg99"/> “effect of present industrial conditions on output of
                    munitions in Russia “which Henderson considers “sufficiently grave to render
                    desirable an exchange of views between the Allied representatives.” Have
                    notified British Ambassador cannot attend at time fixed and suggested change to
                    3d or 5th. He replied Henderson fixed date, absent now, would be informed of my
                    inability to attend on his return. Please cable immediately any information
                    bearing on the subject, what munitions are we furnishing, when shipped.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
